{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\eng\\045.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Reading", "conf": 0.721, "box": [[110, 170], [317, 174], [316, 222], [109, 218]]}, {"text": "Read this poem to see how the poet has used rhyme and rhythm of words to", "conf": 0.949, "box": [[39, 263], [1402, 254], [1402, 304], [39, 313]]}, {"text": "make us feel as if we are really travelling in a train.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[38, 307], [939, 299], [939, 349], [38, 357]]}, {"text": "From a Railway Carriage", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[338, 376], [766, 383], [765, 422], [338, 415]]}, {"text": "Faster than fairies, faster than witches,", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[143, 430], [773, 433], [773, 473], [143, 470]]}, {"text": "Bridges and houses, hedges and ditches;", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[143, 485], [819, 486], [819, 526], [143, 525]]}, {"text": "And charging along like troops in a battle,", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[141, 541], [837, 539], [837, 578], [141, 580]]}, {"text": "All through the meadows the horses and cattle:", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[143, 594], [929, 592], [929, 628], [143, 630]]}, {"text": "Similiesmakework more", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[1111, 594], [1463, 591], [1464, 621], [1111, 624]]}, {"text": "descriptive and enjoyable", "conf": 0.883, "box": [[1110, 635], [1470, 630], [1471, 663], [1111, 668]]}, {"text": "All of the sights of the hill and the plain", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[140, 645], [796, 645], [796, 684], [140, 684]]}, {"text": "Writers and poets use", "conf": 0.874, "box": [[1109, 674], [1419, 672], [1419, 706], [1109, 708]]}, {"text": "Fly as thick as driving rain;", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[140, 700], [576, 698], [576, 738], [140, 740]]}, {"text": "similies to add depth to", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[1107, 715], [1445, 712], [1446, 745], [1107, 748]]}, {"text": "And ever again, in the wink of an eye,", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[136, 753], [760, 754], [760, 793], [136, 792]]}, {"text": "their work.", "conf": 0.803, "box": [[1105, 755], [1259, 753], [1259, 786], [1106, 788]]}, {"text": "Painted stations whistle by.", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[136, 803], [583, 807], [583, 847], [135, 843]]}, {"text": "Here is a child who clambers and scrambles,", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[133, 914], [869, 915], [869, 952], [133, 951]]}, {"text": "All by himself and gathering brambles;", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[131, 967], [778, 968], [778, 1008], [131, 1007]]}, {"text": "Here is a tramp who stands and gazes;", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[129, 1022], [776, 1023], [776, 1060], [129, 1059]]}, {"text": "And there is the green for stringing the daisies!", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[129, 1076], [918, 1076], [918, 1115], [129, 1115]]}, {"text": "Here is a cart run away in the road", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[128, 1130], [703, 1130], [703, 1166], [128, 1166]]}, {"text": "Lumping along with man and load;", "conf": 0.94, "box": [[127, 1185], [713, 1183], [713, 1222], [127, 1224]]}, {"text": "And here is a mill and there is a river:", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[126, 1237], [745, 1238], [745, 1274], [126, 1273]]}, {"text": "Each a glimpse and gone for ever!", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[127, 1291], [698, 1291], [698, 1331], [127, 1331]]}, {"text": "(By: Robert Louis Stevenson)", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[475, 1346], [937, 1343], [937, 1383], [475, 1386]]}, {"text": "The poem also uses a number of similes and alliterations. Read the poem again and", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[20, 1451], [1434, 1450], [1434, 1489], [20, 1490]]}, {"text": "complete the given table with all the similes and alliterations from the poem.", "conf": 0.918, "box": [[18, 1497], [1313, 1496], [1313, 1536], [18, 1537]]}, {"text": "Similes", "conf": 0.856, "box": [[379, 1587], [502, 1587], [502, 1625], [379, 1625]]}, {"text": "Alliterations", "conf": 0.877, "box": [[957, 1587], [1164, 1589], [1163, 1626], [956, 1624]]}, {"text": "40", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[753, 2160], [816, 2160], [816, 2197], [753, 2197]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.861, "box": [[116, 2196], [396, 2196], [396, 2229], [116, 2229]]}]}